30,2,1,talk,Mio,,It seems paying ahead makes people relax more. But I saw that some of us were even afraid to use the cooler this summer.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The bills fluctuate wildly, from 9,000 to nearly 30,000 yen. Also, installing individual meters would be very expensive per room.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The paperwork is a nightmare. Whether it's meters or templates, someone spends ages every month just doing the math and chasing people.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"My suspicions were right. Some rooms use four times more power than others, and the room layout makes heating needs totally unfair.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The payment log is messy. People are paying late because they're arguing about the amounts. It's creating a lot of tension.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, if the rooms are that different, maybe we shouldn't just split it equally?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, but the cost to fix that with meters is too high. We can't just spend thousands of yen upfront.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, if we go for something complex, who is going to manage it? I don't want to spend my evenings on spreadsheets.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, that's why a simple split is bad. It's ""simple"" but it's unfair, which leads to the arguments Misaki mentioned.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Misaki,,Exactly. The current way is causing friction. We need something that stops the monthly disputes.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Mio,,"If we have a fixed rate for the season, would that stop the fighting?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"It would stabilize the monthly cost, but we'd still have to settle the difference at the end of the year.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, is that easier than doing it every single month?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,It's better than ignoring the fact that some of us have freezing rooms and others don't.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"As long as it doesn't lead to one giant argument every December, I'm open to it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Mio,,I just want us to be able to turn the heat on without worrying.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"A flat share is the cheapest to implement, but it doesn't solve the usage gap Shunichi found.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Rin,,I just want the administrative burden to be low.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"A flat share is the most ""fair"" in terms of effort, but the least fair in terms of actual usage.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Misaki,,Let's see the options and decide based on what balances fairness and peace.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
